    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0564" n="392" xml:id="pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8198</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-19T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 20, 1.40
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>634. The Mexican Senate in secret session yesterday defeated the resolution
                    referred to in the Embassy’s telegram 502, October 20, 10 a.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d579-f1"/>, by a 35 to 13 vote.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
